  "description": "Reads an ONNX graph into a DeepSharp network: the one PyTorch's torch.onnx.export writes, by either of its exporters, the one Keras writes with model.export(format=\"onnx\"), or the one tf2onnx converts a TensorFlow SavedModel into. A stack of dense layers — a Gemm, or a MatMul and the Add of its bias — convolutions and poolings along a series, over an image or through a volume, batch and layer normalisations, flattens and activations is lowered onto DeepSharp's layers as DeepSharp's words build them, the loss it answers through handed in. The numbers go in turned as each node declares them — a weight matrix outputs by inputs where Gemm says so, a kernel channels first, a series', an image's or a volume's values flattened channel by channel — and series, images and volumes go in and come out with their channels last, as TensorFlow's already are; they are widened from half precision, rounded from double, read from the file the exporter keeps beside the graph, strictly, every fault named at once where the graph holds it. A branch, and any node no network here is built of — a stride of its own for each axis, a dilated window, a pooling that rounds up, channels in groups — is refused at its node.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
